`data/tensor-shapes.json` is measured from the published weights of the models
listed here, by reading each safetensors file's header (see
scripts/audit-shapes.ts). It records tensor names, their shapes and dtypes, and
counts derived from them. It contains no weights, no parameter values and no code
from any model, and the files themselves are never downloaded — only the header
at the front of each one.

Those checkpoints are released under terms of their own, and this repository
grants nothing in respect of them: Apache-2.0 and MIT for most, and for the rest
the Gemma Terms of Use, the NVIDIA Nemotron Open Model License, and the Llama 3.1,
3.2 and 3.3 Community Licenses. Each model's own entry links its license. Anyone
using a model must go to that license, not to this one.

What CC BY 4.0 covers here is our own work: the measuring, the selection of what
to record, and the arrangement. The measurements themselves are facts about
published files and we make no claim on the facts.

Raw benchmark values referenced in provenance entries remain the work of their
cited sources and are reproduced under their respective terms; sources whose
terms forbid republication are cited by link only and their values are never
stored here.
